Commands that manage olrd. Unlike the rest of olr, these do not go
through olrd's API — they work when it is stopped or unresponsive.

Usage:
  olr daemon [command]

Available Commands:
  listen      Serve the web UI on a network address
  restart     Restart olrd
  start       Start olrd
  status      Report whether olrd is running
  stop        Stop olrd

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for daemon

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")

Use "olr daemon [command] --help" for more information about a command.
